      "showAdvanced": null,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Qwen-Image-2.1 Head Swap (BFS)\n\nModelos usados (ja baixados):\n- `models/diffusion_models/qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors`\n- `models/text_encoders/qwen3vl_8b_fp8_heretic.safetensors`\n- `models/vae/qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors`\n- `models/loras/bfs_head_v1.1_qwen_2.1.safetensors`\n- `models/loras/Qwen-Image-2.1-viggle-turbo-v0.2.1-6step-lora-r128.safetensors`\n\n### Como usar\n1. **Image 1** = corpo/cena (a pessoa cujo rosto sera trocado).\n2. **Image 2** = cabeca/rosto que voce quer colar.\n3. Mantenha esta ordem (o autor do BFS exige corpo primeiro, rosto depois).\n4. O prompt ja esta preenchido. Nao inverta as imagens.\n\n### Forcas dos LoRAs\n- **BFS Head V1.1**: 1.0 (ajuste para equilibrar identidade x suavidade da pele).\n- **Viggle Turbo**: 1.0 (mantenha 1.0; e um destilado de 6 passos).\n\n### Velocidade vs qualidade\n- **Turbo (este workflow)**: 6 passos, sem CFG, rapido.\n- Para edicoes dificeis, use o arquivo **\"...Quality...\"**: KSampler 25 passos, cfg 1, euler/simple.\n\n### Memoria\n- Tudo roda em int8 (~17 GB de checkpoints); o ComfyUI faz offload para a RAM.\n- Se faltar VRAM na 1a execucao, baixe `resolution` para 1024 e feche apps que usam a GPU.\n\n### Prompt\n- O prompt do BFS ja esta no no \"Prompt (BFS Head Swap)\". Ele e usado literalmente\n  (o ramo opcional de aprimoramento de prompt do template oficial foi removido para\n  manter o texto exato e acelerar a execucao).\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Qwen-Image-2.1 Viggle Turbo · image edit\n\nUses the same files and custom nodes as the text-to-image workflow (see its note). Keep euler, BasicGuider (no CFG) and the unmerged LoRA node at strength 1.0.\n\n- **Example references** `woman2.webp` and `cat.webp` are in the model repo's `comfyui/input/`; copy them into `ComfyUI/input/`, or load your own.\n- **References** go into *TextEncodeQwenImage21* as `image_1`, `image_2`, …; connecting one adds another slot. In the prompt, call them \"image 1\", \"image 2\" (or `<image1>`, `<image2>`).\n- **Output size** follows image 1, at about 1 MP (diffusers follows the *last* reference; put the image whose framing you want first). Turn on *Custom output size* to use the *Output size* node instead; a size other than image 1's can shift the edit.\n- **QwenImage21Cache** stores the reference part of the sequence once instead of recomputing it every step. At `dtype = default` it is lossless.\n- **Prompt enhancer** works as in text to image, with the official edit rewriter. The rewriter sees image 1 and image 2 (for this, image 2 is resized and cropped to image 1's size). With a single reference, connect image 1 straight to *TextGenerate → image* and delete *Batch Images*. For an instruction in Chinese, change the line in *PE request* to `（描述用中文写。）`.\n"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
